    <text><list><item>Wheeze, cough and breathlessness this winter, for about three months: symptoms on three or four days a week, waking with cough and a tight chest about twice a month, breathless climbing the hill streets in cold air; worse with cold wind, kitchen and fireplace smoke, and colds; called a weak chest and asthma since childhood but never tested or treated. Asthma to be confirmed with spirometry before and after bronchodilator and FeNO: active, confirmed [S]</item></list></text>

